    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. but i'm getting a lot of pushback from the business community and some other council members. they're arguing that a lottery system is actually more \"equitable\" because it treats everyone as an equal under the law and avoids the bureaucracy of constant income verification. plus, some say transit-based allocation is better for the city's overall long-term efficiency. \n\nwhy do you think the income-based approach is definitely better than those other two?",
