      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The income-based approach is superior because it directly targets the root of the housing crisis: income inequality. A lottery system, while seemingly fair, often benefits those who are already better off, as they have more resources to navigate the system. Transit-based allocation, though efficient, can inadvertently favor those who live closer to transit hubs, potentially neglecting those in more remote areas who also need affordable housing. The income-based method ensures that the most vulnerable populations are prioritized, fostering a more just and equitable society. It's not just about fairness; it's about addressing systemic issues that perpetuate inequality.",
      "source": "target",
